# #!/bin/sh
# # Local validation policy (docs/ops/validation-policy.md) pre-push tier: a full
# # project typecheck (not diff-scoped — tsc has no such mode, this re-checks the
# # whole graph, just via the same --incremental flags as package.json's
# # `check:types:incremental` script, kept in sync manually, so a cache warmed by
# # pre-commit makes this fast) + tests related to what changed vs. the branch's
# # upstream (that part IS diff-scoped, via `vitest --changed`). Full repo-wide lint
# # and the full test suite stay in CI — this hook deliberately does not re-run them.
# #
# # Validation output runs through `rtk` (~/.claude/RTK.md) when it's on PATH, for
# # cheaper output when an agent is reading this hook's output. tsc is invoked as
# # `rtk tsc` directly (not via `pnpm exec`/`pnpm run`) so rtk's dedicated
# # grouped-error filter actually fires — falls back to `pnpm exec tsc` when rtk
# # isn't installed. `git rev-parse` below is NOT routed through rtk — its output is
# # parsed into $UPSTREAM, and rtk's compacted format isn't guaranteed parseable the
# # same way.
# #
# # Tolerant by design, same as .githooks/pre-commit: never block a push just
# # because the repo isn't `pnpm install`ed yet.
